{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q01629","uniProtkbId":"IFM2_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Interferon-induced transmembrane protein 2"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Dispanin subfamily A member 2c"},"shortNames":[{"value":"DSPA2c"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"Interferon-inducible protein 1-8D"}}]},"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19544527"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20064371"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20534863"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"20943977"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21177806"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21253575"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22479637"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26354436"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33239446"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33270927"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"33563656"}],"value":"IFN-induced antiviral protein which inhibits the entry of viruses to the host cell cytoplasm, permitting endocytosis, but preventing subsequent viral fusion and release of viral contents into the cytosol (PubMed:26354436, PubMed:33563656). Active against multiple viruses, including influenza A virus, SARS coronaviruses (SARS-CoV and SARS-CoV-2), Marburg virus (MARV), Ebola virus (EBOV), Dengue virus (DNV), West Nile virus (WNV), human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1), hepatitis C virus (HCV) and vesicular stomatitis virus (VSV) (PubMed:26354436, PubMed:33239446, PubMed:33270927, PubMed:33563656). Can inhibit: influenza virus hemagglutinin protein-mediated viral entry, MARV and EBOV GP1,2-mediated viral entry, SARS-CoV and SARS-CoV-2 S protein-mediated viral entry and VSV G protein-mediated viral entry (PubMed:33563656). Induces cell cycle arrest and mediates apoptosis by caspase activation and in p53-independent manner. In hepatocytes, IFITM proteins act in a coordinated manner to restrict HCV infection by targeting the endocytosed HCV virion for lysosomal degradation (PubMed:26354436). IFITM2 and IFITM3 display anti-HCV activity that may complement the anti-HCV activity of IFITM1 by inhibiting the late stages of HCV entry, possibly in a coordinated manner by trapping the virion in the endosomal pathway and targeting it for degradation at the lysosome (PubMed:26354436)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"33563656"}],"value":"Cell membrane","id":"SL-0039"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Single-pass type II membrane protein","id":"SL-9906"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26354436"}],"value":"Lysosome membrane","id":"SL-0157"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Single-pass type II membrane protein","id":"SL-9906"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"26354436"}],"value":"Late endosome membrane","id":"SL-0151"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Single-pass type II membrane protein","id":"SL-9906"}}]}],"features":[{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":107,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":127,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Modified residue","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-acetylmethionine","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PubMed","id":"20068231"}]},{"type":"Modified residue","location":{"start":{"value":19,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":19,"modifier":